-- title:
--   Eisenstein character mod m on the weight-two Hecke algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ and $m$ be natural numbers with $p$ prime and $m \ge 2$. Write $\mathbb{T}(p)$ for [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra p 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(p)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid p$ together with $U_q$ for primes $q \mid p$, and write $\mathbb{T} =$ `HeckeAlg` for the polynomial ring $\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$. Let `eisensteinIdeal p` be the kernel of the $\mathbb{Z}$-algebra map $\mathbb{T} \to \mathbb{Z}$ sending $X_\ell \mapsto 1$ when $\ell \mid p$ and $X_\ell \mapsto 1 + \ell$ otherwise, and let `heckeProj p` $: \mathbb{T} \to \mathbb{T}(p)$ be the $\mathbb{Z}$-algebra map sending $X_\ell \mapsto U_\ell$ when $\ell \mid p$ and $X_\ell \mapsto T_\ell$ otherwise. Assume that for every integer $c$ whose image in $\mathbb{T}(p)$ lies in the ideal generated by the image of the Eisenstein ideal under `heckeProj p` together with $m$, one has $m \mid c$ in $\mathbb{Z}$. Then there is a ring homomorphism $\chi : \mathbb{T}(p) \to \mathbb{Z}/m$ that vanishes on every element of the ideal generated by the image of the Eisenstein ideal, and satisfies $\chi(c) = c \bmod m$ for every integer $c$.
--
--   This is the construction of the Eisenstein character modulo $m$ in the sense of Mazur: a ring homomorphism from the weight-two Hecke algebra of level $p$ onto $\mathbb{Z}/m$ killing the Eisenstein ideal, existing exactly when the integers meet that ideal (enlarged by $m$) only in $m\mathbb{Z}$. It feeds the construction of mod $m$ Eisenstein eigenforms in [`CuspForm.exists_qIntegral_eisenstein_eigen_mod_of_injective`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_qIntegral_eisenstein_eigen_mod_of_injective).
-- source:
